This is mildly annoying, since you can't change padding before your window exists, but after you create it the bitmap already has a size that's based on default padding. I'd generally make them this way (assuming you want no padding in a window with size 640x25):
JavaScript:
let padding = Window_Base.prototype.standardPadding();
this._testGauge = new Window_Base(0, 0, 640 + padding * 2, 25 + padding * 2);
this._testGauge.standardPadding = () => 0;
this._testGauge.padding = 0;
this._testGauge.move(0, 0, 640, 25);

