I ran into this with one of my other plugins - there's a Window_Base.createContents() which resizes the (creates a new) contents bitmap based on the current width and height.
So, since I'm allowing user-provided images which I don't know the dimensions of ahead of time, I should be able to do (haven't tested it yet):
JavaScript:
let padding = Window_Base.prototype.standardPadding();
this._testGauge = new Window_Base();
this._testGauge.standardPadding = () => 0;
this._testGauge.padding = 0;

this.addChild(this._testGauge);
this._testGauge.opacity = 0;
this._testGauge._frame = new Sprite_Base();
this._testGauge._frame.bitmap = ImageManager.loadPicture("meter-frame");
this._testGauge.addChild(this._testGauge._frame);

this._testGauge.contentsWidth = () => this._testGauge._frame.bitmap.width;
this._testGauge.contentsHeight = () => this._testGauge._frame.bitmap.height;

this._testGauge.createContents();
